    <desc>Save the text of a terminal, with its scrollback, to a file.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Save contents</title>

<p>You can save all the text of a terminal, including its scrollback, to a
  text file. This may be useful if you have to submit the terminal output as
  debugging information.</p>
  <steps>
<item><p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and select <gui style="menuitem">Save Contents…</gui>.</p></item>
<item><p>Choose a folder and enter a file name.</p></item>
<item><p>Click <gui style="button">Save</gui>.</p></item>
</steps>

  <p>The window stays usable while long scrollbacks are saved.</p>

